issues/6284#issuecomment-820621316","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/6284","id":820621316,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDgyMDYyMTMxNg==","user":{"login":"wmolicki","id":3396702,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTY3MDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3396702?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki","html_url":"https://github.com/wmolicki","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-04-15T17:56:12Z","updated_at":"2021-04-15T17:56:12Z","body":"Hi, thanks for responding quickly.\r\n\r\n(I'm only using session.execute(query) while debugging to get the actual query from the cursor (with params filled in) - glad that discovered potential issue)\r\n\r\nI tried to provide a better example, and found out my problem was caused by using the same session object for creating db fixtures and then for querying (without clearing the session)- so the objects were present in original session (and they didn't have query_expression loaded) - see the following example:\r\n\r\n```py\r\nsession.add(User(id=1, name='bogdan'))\r\nsession.commit()\r\n\r\n_ = session.query(User).all()\r\n\r\nq = session.query(\r\n    User\r\n).options(\r\n    with_expression(\r\n        User.company_name, literal('github').label('company_name'),\r\n    )\r\n)\r\n\r\nresult = q.all()\r\n\r\nfor obj in result:\r\n    print(f'{obj.company_name=}')\r\n```\r\n\r\nOn 1.3 this code will return `company_name='github'`, and on 1.4 `company_name=None`. Not sure if that is intended.\r\n\r\n>note above that this is still not the \"main purpose\" of with_expression(). if you want a certain expression in a Core select you just ask for it, that is, the \"legit\" way to write your query would be:\r\n\r\nYes, this was only meant as simplest example, we do all kinds of crazy things with this query_expressions (like putting CASE statements in there) probably also not intended usage","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/820621316/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"wmolicki","id":3396702,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTY3MDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3396702?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki","html_url":"https://github.com/wmolicki","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wmolicki/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/820625278","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/6284#issuecomment-820625278","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/6284","id":820625278,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDgyMDYyNTI3OA==","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-04-15T18:02:32Z","updated_at":"2021-04-15T18:02:32Z","body":"Try out 1.4.8, because what is happening there is that your first query will not include \"company_name\", so the attribute is unloaded, then on the next query, you specified it so it gets loaded.   The reason this isnt working in 1.4.7 is due to part of #6259 , where I identified that the query_expression was being rendered as NULL every time.\r\n\r\nBut also, if you want that query_expr to load guaranteed, you would best be using [populate existing](https://docs.sqlalchemy.org/en/14/orm/queryguide.html#populate-existing).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/820625278/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":